--- mailbox/openapi send schema ---
/v1/mailbox/messages {
  "get": {
    "tags": [
      "mailbox"
    ],
    "summary": "Poll",
    "description": "Poll your mailbox: mail sent **to** your address with `id > since_id`, oldest first.\n\nEverything reaches you here: customer requests, carrier bids, rate desk answers, booking\nconfirmations, airline tariff mails and tracking questions. You can also get each new mail\npushed to your own endpoint (`PUT /v1/mailbox/webhook`); the poll stays complete either way.\n\n- Keep `next_since_id` and pass it as `since_id` on the next call. Ids only grow, so you\n  never miss or repeat a mail.\n- At most `limit` mails per call (max 200).\n- **Limit:** one poll every 5 seconds per team key; a faster poll gets 429 with\n  `Retry-After`. Limits may be tuned. Mail is stored the moment it is sent; for the fastest\n  delivery use the webhook push.\n- `references` lists the ids of a thread from its first mail down to the parent.\n- `attachments` lists id, filename, content type and size; download each with\n  `GET /v1/mailbox/messages/{message_id}/attachments/{attachment_id}`.",
    "operationId": "poll_v1_mailbox_messages_get",
    "security": [
      {
        "Team key": []
      }
    ],
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "since_id",
        "in": "query",
        "required": false,
        "schema": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0,
          "description": "Return messages with id greater than this",
          "default": 0,
          "title": "Since Id"
        },
        "description": "Return messages with id greater than this"
      },
      {
        "name": "limit",
        "in": "query",
        "required": false,
        "schema": {
          "type": "integer",
          "maximum": 200,
          "minimum": 1,
          "default": 100,
          "title": "Limit"
        }
      }
    ],
    "responses": {
      "200": {
        "description": "Successful Response",
        "content": {
          "application/json": {
            "schema": {
              "type": "object",
              "additionalProperties": true,
              "title": "Response Poll V1 Mailbox Messages Get"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "422": {
        "description": "Validation Error",
        "content": {
          "application/json": {
            "schema": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "post": {
    "tags": [
      "mailbox"
    ],
    "summary": "Send",
    "description": "Send a mail from your address. Returns 201 with the stored mail, shaped like a poll item.\n\n- **Reply in the thread:** set `in_reply_to` to the id of the mail you answer. A quote\n  counts only as a reply in a thread one of our customers started. One quote per\n  request is judged, normally your first. `in_reply_to` must be a mail you sent or received, else 404.\n- **Who you can write to:** customers, the airlines and truckers in the start kit's\n  carrier list, `ratedesk@hackloop.mail`, `tracking@hackloop.mail` and any other outside\n  sender that mailed you. Any other address, including another team's, gets 422.\n- **Attachments:** `[{\"filename\", \"content_type\", \"content_base64\"}]`, at most 5 per mail\n  and 10 MB each. Allowed file types: pdf, xlsx, xls, csv, txt, png, jpg, docx.\n- **Limit:** 60 mails per minute per team key, then 429. Limits may be tuned.",
    "operationId": "send_v1_mailbox_messages_post",
    "security": [
      {
        "Team key": []
      }
    ],
    "requestBody": {
      "required": true,
      "content": {
        "application/json": {
          "schema": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/MessageIn"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "responses": {
      "201": {
        "description": "Successful Response",
        "content": {
          "application/json": {
            "schema": {
              "type": "object",
              "additionalProperties": true,
              "title": "Response Send V1 Mailbox Messages Post"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "422": {
        "description": "Validation Error",
        "content": {
          "application/json": {
            "schema": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
